From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] nautilus: initialize the shared Luma surface before windows

Filer already links the shared Luma UI and consumes its components, but the
library was reached only by view-specific paths. A normal non-empty folder
could therefore create its first window before Luma UI registered the native
surface binding, leaving Frost and Glass opaque.

Initialize the shared platform immediately after GtkApplication startup, when
the display and default application both exist and before Nautilus creates a
window. This is toolkit adoption at the application's native startup boundary;
it does not add a Filer-local material implementation.

---
 src/nautilus-application.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nautilus-application.c b/src/nautilus-application.c
--- a/src/nautilus-application.c
+++ b/src/nautilus-application.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "nautilus-application.h"
 
 #include <adwaita.h>
+#include <luma-ui.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <gdk/gdk.h>
 #include <gio/gio.h>
@@ -981,6 +982,8 @@ nautilus_application_startup (GApplication *app)
      */
     G_APPLICATION_CLASS (nautilus_application_parent_class)->startup (G_APPLICATION (self));
 
+    luma_init ();
+
     g_assert (display == NULL || gdk_display_get_default () == display);
 
     gtk_window_set_default_icon_name (APPLICATION_ID);
-- 
2.54.0
